## Data Persistence with UserDefaults

```swift
class SettingsManager {
    static let shared = SettingsManager()

    private let defaults = UserDefaults.standard

    var isDarkMode: Bool {
        get { defaults.bool(forKey: "isDarkMode") }
        set { defaults.set(newValue, forKey: "isDarkMode") }
    }

    var username: String? {
        get { defaults.string(forKey: "username") }
        set { defaults.set(newValue, forKey: "username") }
    }
}

// Usage
SettingsManager.shared.username = "John"
let name = SettingsManager.shared.username
```

## Networking

```swift
struct User: Codable {
    let id: Int
    let name: String
    let email: String
}

class NetworkManager {
    func fetchUsers() async throws -> [User] {
        let url = URL(string: "https://api.example.com/users")!
        let (data, _) = try await URLSession.shared.data(from: url)
        let users = try JSONDecoder().decode([User].self, from: data)
        return users
    }
}

// Usage in SwiftUI
struct UsersView: View {
    @State private var users: [User] = []

    var body: some View {
        List(users) { user in
            VStack(alignment: .leading) {
                Text(user.name)
                    .font(.headline)
                Text(user.email)
                    .font(.caption)
                    .foregroundColor(.gray)
            }
        }
        .task {
            do {
                users = try await NetworkManager().fetchUsers()
            } catch {
                print("Error: \(error)")
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Best Practices

1. ✅ **Use SwiftUI** - Modern, declarative UI
2. ✅ **Follow Apple's HIG** - Human Interface Guidelines
3. ✅ **Handle errors properly** - Use try-catch for safety
4. ✅ **Test on real devices** - Simulators miss some issues
5. ✅ **Use SF Symbols** - Built-in icon library
6. ✅ **Optimize for different devices** - iPhone, iPad support
7. ✅ **Follow naming conventions** - Clear, Swift-style names

## Common Mistakes

❌ **Force unwrapping** - Can cause crashes
❌ **Not using @State** - UI won't update
❌ **Blocking main thread** - Use async/await
❌ **Hardcoding strings** - Use localization
❌ **Ignoring memory management** - Be careful with retain cycles

## App Store Submission

1. Enroll in Apple Developer Program ($99/year)
2. Create App Store Connect account
3. Prepare app icons and screenshots
4. Write app description
5. Submit for review
6. Wait for approval (usually 1-2 days)

